+# Feature Specification: JSON Patch
+
+**Feature Branch**: `002-json-patch`
+**Created**: 2026-11-12
+**Status**: Draft
+**Input**: "Implement JSON Patch (RFC 6902) with add, remove, replace, move, copy, test. Export applyPatch(document, patch) from src/index.ts; returns a new document, never mutates input; throws when the patch is invalid or an operation fails."
+
+**Standard**: JSON Patch, RFC 6902 — §3 (document structure), §4.1–4.6 (operations), §5 (error handling, atomicity). Pointers follow RFC 6901 (§3, §4). `test` equality follows RFC 6902 §4.6.
+
+## Requirements
+
+- **FR-001**: `applyPatch` applies operations sequentially, each to the result of the previous (§3).
+- **FR-002**: The patch MUST be an array of objects, each with a string `op` among the six and a string `path` (§4); `add`/`replace`/`test` need a `value` member (`null` is valid); `move`/`copy` need a string `from`. Unknown members are ignored; anything else is an invalid patch.
+- **FR-003**: `add` (§4.1): empty path replaces the whole document; object parent: adds or replaces the member; array parent: inserts before the index (`0..length`) or appends with `-`. Parent must exist.
+- **FR-004**: `remove` (§4.2) and `replace` (§4.3): the target MUST exist (array index `< length`, `-` is not valid).
+- **FR-005**: `move` (§4.4): `from` MUST exist; it is removed then added at `path`; `from` MUST NOT be a proper prefix of `path`.
+- **FR-006**: `copy` (§4.5): `from` MUST exist; a deep copy is added at `path`.
+- **FR-007**: `test` (§4.6): deep equality (objects unordered, arrays ordered, numbers by value, `null` distinct from missing); failure is an error.
+- **FR-008**: Errors are atomic (§5): on any failure the input is unchanged and an error is thrown. The input document and patch are never mutated; the result shares no structure with either.
+- **FR-009**: `__proto__`, `constructor`, `prototype` keys MUST NOT pollute prototypes; they are ordinary member names.
+- **FR-010**: Failures throw `PatchError` with code `INVALID_PATCH` or `OPERATION_FAILED`.
+
+## Out of scope
+JSON Pointer URI fragment form; JSON Merge Patch (RFC 7396).
